(src/calendar.vox: the meeting days; the start-date rule; the moment and
 label of meeting N.)

see date version "0.1" from "date.lib".

(Change the congregation's two meeting days here; nothing else names them.)
a number called 'the midweek meeting day' is 3.
a number called 'the weekend meeting day' is 7.

a number called 'meeting count' is 0.
a number called 'the first midweek moment' is 0.

To 'the week of meeting' with a number called 'meeting number'.
  Return a number, {'meeting number' add 1} divide 2.

To 'meeting is at the weekend' with a number called 'meeting number'.
  a number called 'the remainder' is 'meeting number' modulo 2.
  Return a boolean, 'the remainder' is 0.

To 'the kind of meeting' with a number called 'meeting number'.
  If 'meeting is at the weekend' of 'meeting number' then, Return a text, "weekend".
  Return a text, "midweek".

To 'the moment of meeting' with a number called 'meeting number'.
  a number called 'the week' is 'the week of meeting' of 'meeting number'.
  a number called 'weeks after the first' is 'the week' subtract 1.
  a number called 'the midweek moment of this week' is 'weeks later' of 'the first midweek moment' and 'weeks after the first'.
  If 'meeting is at the weekend' of 'meeting number' then,
    a number called 'days from midweek to weekend' is 'the weekend meeting day' subtract 'the midweek meeting day',
    Return a number, 'days later' of 'the midweek moment of this week' and 'days from midweek to weekend'.
  Return a number, 'the midweek moment of this week'.

To 'the long date of' with a number called moment.
  a text called 'the long date layout' is "%a %e %b %Y".
  Return a text, 'the moment written as' of moment and 'the long date layout'.

To 'the short date of' with a number called moment.
  a text called 'the short date layout' is "%-d %b %Y".
  Return a text, 'the moment written as' of moment and 'the short date layout'.

To 'the label of meeting' with a number called 'meeting number'.
  a number called moment is 'the moment of meeting' of 'meeting number'.
  a text called kind is 'the kind of meeting' of 'meeting number'.
  a text called 'the label date layout' is "%a %-d %b %Y".
  a text called 'the label date' is 'the moment written as' of moment and 'the label date layout'.
  Return a text, "{'the label date'} {kind}".

To 'the default first midweek moment'.
  a number called now is 'the moment now'.
  a number called 'the start of this month' is 'the start of the month of' of now.
  a number called 'the start of next month' is 'months later' of 'the start of this month' and 1.
  Return a number, 'the weekday on or after' of 'the start of next month' and 'the midweek meeting day'.

To 'the first midweek moment typed as' with a text called 'the start date as typed'.
  If 'the start date as typed' is empty then,
    a number called 'the typed moment' is 'the default first midweek moment'.
  Otherwise, if 'reads as a moment' of 'the start date as typed' then,
    a number called 'the typed moment' is 'the moment read from' of 'the start date as typed'.
  Otherwise, if 'reads as a description' of 'the start date as typed' then,
    a number called now is 'the moment now',
    a number called 'the typed moment' is 'the moment described by' of 'the start date as typed' and now.
  Otherwise,
    Print "scheduler: cannot read the start date \"{'the start date as typed'}\"",
    Exit 1.
  a number called 'the start of that day' is 'the start of the day of' of 'the typed moment'.
  a number called weekday is 'the weekday of' of 'the start of that day'.
  If weekday is not 'the midweek meeting day' then,
    a text called 'the actual weekday name' is 'the weekday name of' of weekday,
    a text called 'the required weekday name' is 'the weekday name of' of 'the midweek meeting day',
    a text called 'the long date' is 'the long date of' of 'the start of that day',
    Print "scheduler: {'the long date'} is a {'the actual weekday name'}, but the first midweek meeting must be a {'the required weekday name'}",
    Exit 1.
  Return a number, 'the start of that day'.
